                <pb facs="0384" n="212" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg212"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111Y2/2</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-07T11:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 7, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 8, 5 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>399. Department’s 290, February 24 [<hi rendition="#italic">27</hi>], 3
                        p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d253-f1"/> and 292 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >291</hi>], February 27, 4 p.m. Spanish Ambassador Berlin reports that
                    Spanish Embassy doctor visited <hi rendition="#italic">Yarrowdale</hi> prisoners
                    at Brandenburg on 1st instant and stated that conditions were as reported by
                    German authorities and approved of the quarantine. The case of typhus occurred
                    on February 20 and quarantine will end March 7 unless new cases occur. The
                    doctor said men complained of diet and were glad to hear of approaching release
                    and had no other complaint. Of the 57 Americans only 5 were in the hospital
                    suffering from <pb facs="0385" n="213" xml:id="pg213"/> slight colds and 5 men
                    of different nationality are under medical observation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
